00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:16,954
[Vital Anne (President)] I know this is a lease, and, um, would it, um, how would the Finances or numbers worked out if we had owned the property or have a property that could be used.

190
00:31:17,018 --> 00:31:17,516
[Ayessa Potts] I wondered.

191
00:31:17,516 --> 00:31:20,484
[Dan Trudel] So in essence, what would a property like that cost?

192
00:31:20,484 --> 00:31:25,056
[Vital Anne (President)] Or not that, but build something among our— in our own building?

193
00:31:25,056 --> 00:32:01,311
[Dan Trudel] Yeah, I mean, it really— it just depends on the size of what you're going to build. Um, you know, going right up a new build or even a renovation is probably $350 a square foot. So something like this will be $350 per square foot times 8,000. I mean, it'd be a pretty sizable number to build, which, as we look at Athens and other spaces around the district, and, you know, we're constantly assessing every year, but that's what we want to look into. Get this lease, get them the space to operate for now, and then let us kind of go through the entire district and ultimately decide what might be the most appropriate avenue internally.

194
00:32:01,311 --> 00:32:08,083
