267
00:50:36,341 --> 00:50:36,519
[Ayessa Potts] Okay.

268
00:50:36,843 --> 00:51:13,892
[Dr. Richard Machesky] No, I mean, well, we can— we will continue to be strategic in terms of cutting around the edges and reducing, tightening. And that's where I think that's where important for folks to understand this go-round, we really tightened. So we tightened ratios where we could. We were able to work within current contractual agreements and so forth in order to kind of constrict.

269
00:51:13,892 --> 00:51:14,909
[Ayessa Potts] Okay.

270
00:51:16,584 --> 00:51:26,450
[Dr. Richard Machesky] But yes, it would likely— we're likely talking about programming cuts, which equates to people, as hard as that is to say.

