l this summer, we stripped and updated the auxiliary gym floor, and so that is fully functional. That happened at the beginning of the summer, so we're really happy to have that space for our Troy High students when they come back. We've put in place a fob system at Troy High with some new badges that will be used by our teachers to be able to access that building. So Troy High was one of our only buildings that didn't have fob access. And so that will be very helpful as we think about safety and security across the district. Those badges are also badges that we're using here at central office. We'll be using at services, and we will be rolling out across the district. So that links really to a lot of our safety and security work that we've been taking on this summer. Also at Troy High, the Troy High track is underway. So that began even before the end of the school year and will continue all the way through and Probably past tryouts. So as we hit mid-August, so we do anticipate a little bit of a disruption as we hit the beginning of tryouts, but we do know that by the week of August 24th, we'll be ready to go with the Troy High track. So before we start football season—

