lding. That is a nice space for them to be while we wait for the formalization of that drive-in. The gym at Smith is one of the last spaces to be finished. That is underway, and in a minute here I'm going to show you some pictures of where that is. But we anticipate almost all of the significant components of Smith being complete that week of August 17th as we welcome students. Right now our learning communities, our classroom spaces, are complete. They're beautiful. The furniture is being delivered. They're cleaning their way out of those spaces. Our bathrooms rooms are fully functional, so we can host people over there. We just don't have full occupancy of that building yet, and we are trying to stay out of everyone's way so that they can go as fast as they can in order to get us ready. Um, we're working through all the safety and security in that building as well, building out maps, working with Troy Police Department, making sure that the partnerships with all of our different agencies are included as we get ready to have students in that building in that At Boulan, Boulan Park Middle School is a shell of a building, and I mean that in the kindest way possible. For anyone who's been over there, you can see right through it. We are very excited as they begin that work at Boulan over the next 14 months to build out a new school with learning communities for our middle school students. Larson is in the finalization process. Larson will be very similar to Boulan. There'll be a few tweaks because we A few programmatic differences between those 2 buildings, specifically in our categorical programs and special education. But we're also working on what might be enhancements on the outside and the outside spaces at Larson and at Boland. So those are under leg. And then finally, our bid for Athens and the new Athens build will go out at the end of September, and that is for the 3-story academic addition that will be built in that parking lot in the back. So lots of work g